1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,950
Every video on this channel is made by a system.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:07,550
One that scripts, produces and publishes, in about a day.

3
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:09,817
Today, I'm opening it up.

4
00:00:09,867 --> 00:00:12,850
The exact faceless content pipeline.

5
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:15,283
The format, the tools, the money,

6
00:00:15,333 --> 00:00:19,550
and the mistakes to avoid. Let's get into it.

7
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:23,283
Everything starts with one decision. Your format.

8
00:00:23,333 --> 00:00:27,150
One niche. One video style. One schedule.

9
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:29,917
This channel? AI money topics.

10
00:00:29,967 --> 00:00:33,117
Bold text visuals. One video a week.

11
00:00:33,167 --> 00:00:34,783
Why so strict?

12
00:00:34,833 --> 00:00:39,383
Because a repeatable format means every video makes the next one faster.

13
00:00:39,433 --> 00:00:43,050
And the algorithm learns exactly who to show you to.

14
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:46,583
Pick a lane before you touch a single tool.

15
00:00:46,633 --> 00:00:48,750
Next, the script.

16
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:51,650
And here's the part most people get wrong.

17
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:55,283
AI writes the draft. It shouldn't write the ideas.

18
00:00:55,333 --> 00:00:58,817
You bring the topic, the numbers, and the opinion.

19
00:00:58,867 --> 00:01:01,217
AI helps you structure it.

20
00:01:01,267 --> 00:01:05,250
A hook in the first ten seconds. One clear promise.

21
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:08,617
Short sentences. And a payoff at the end.

22
00:01:08,667 --> 00:01:10,550
Read it out loud once.

23
00:01:10,600 --> 00:01:15,117
If a sentence sounds like a robot wrote it, rewrite it.

24
00:01:15,167 --> 00:01:18,850
Now production. And it's simpler than you think.

25
00:01:18,900 --> 00:01:23,550
Visuals? Bold text slides, generated from the script.

26
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:26,117
Voiceover? Text to speech,

27
00:01:26,167 --> 00:01:29,750
or your own voice, if you have twenty quiet minutes.

28
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:31,517
Captions burned in,

29
00:01:31,567 --> 00:01:34,050
because most people watch on mute.

30
00:01:34,100 --> 00:01:37,650
Tools change every month. The system doesn't.

31
00:01:37,700 --> 00:01:40,183
Script in. Video out.

32
00:01:40,233 --> 00:01:43,317
Aim for under half a day per video.

33
00:01:43,367 --> 00:01:45,417
The upload is half the game.

34
00:01:45,467 --> 00:01:49,483
Your title and thumbnail decide whether anyone clicks at all.

35
00:01:49,533 --> 00:01:52,150
Three or four bold words on the thumbnail.

36
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:55,283
A title that makes one specific promise.

37
00:01:55,333 --> 00:01:59,183
Then chapters, captions and tags, for search.

38
00:01:59,233 --> 00:02:02,983
And one detail people skip. The first comment.

39
00:02:03,033 --> 00:02:06,983
Pin a question, and answer every reply for the first hour.

40
00:02:07,033 --> 00:02:09,650
The algorithm notices.

41
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:13,017
So what does it pay? Here's the honest math.

42
00:02:13,067 --> 00:02:17,217
Ads need a thousand subscribers, and four thousand watch hours.

43
00:02:17,267 --> 00:02:18,450
In a money niche,

44
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:22,517
that's ten to thirty dollars per thousand views. Decent.

45
00:02:22,567 --> 00:02:24,783
But the real money arrives later.

46
00:02:24,833 --> 00:02:27,183
Sponsors, who pay per video.

47
00:02:27,233 --> 00:02:30,450
And affiliate links, that pay every month.

48
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:34,850
Most channels see their first real dollar around month three to six.

49
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:37,083
Plan for that.

50
00:02:37,133 --> 00:02:38,850
And the reality check.

51
00:02:38,900 --> 00:02:42,217
Your first twenty videos are practice in public.

52
00:02:42,267 --> 00:02:45,383
Views will be embarrassing. That's normal.

53
00:02:45,433 --> 00:02:48,883
Watch your retention graph, not your view count.

54
00:02:48,933 --> 00:02:51,250
Find the second where people leave,

55
00:02:51,300 --> 00:02:53,717
and fix it in the next video.

56
00:02:53,767 --> 00:02:56,617
The creators who win aren't more talented.

57
00:02:56,667 --> 00:02:59,383
They just didn't stop.

58
00:02:59,433 --> 00:03:01,217
Your ninety day plan.

59
00:03:01,267 --> 00:03:05,483
Month one. Pick your format, and publish four videos.

60
00:03:05,533 --> 00:03:08,083
Month two. Study retention,

61
00:03:08,133 --> 00:03:10,283
and double down on what worked.

62
00:03:10,333 --> 00:03:13,283
Month three. Apply for monetization,

63
00:03:13,333 --> 00:03:15,883
and pitch your first affiliate deal.

64
00:03:15,933 --> 00:03:21,450
Next week. AI digital products. From zero, to your first sale.

65
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:24,750
Subscribe, and I'll see you there.

